<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Calkiní</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Calkiní is a town in the north of the Mexican state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campeche">Campeche</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yucatan-peninsula">Yucatán Peninsula</a>. After the fall of Mayapan around 1441 it became the leading town of Ah Canul, a Maya province governed by lords of the Canul lineage. Its colonial Maya chronicle, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/codex-of-calkini">Codex of Calkiní</a>, records the lineages of the province and the arrival of the Spanish.</p></div>
